abstract: |
  The Algebra of the Extended Indeterminate (AEI) is a revolutionary computational 
  and mathematical framework that treats 0/0 as a generative algebraic unit I, 
  rather than an undefined error. This system extends traditional algebra with:
  
  - Cardinal arithmetic where κ ⊖ κ = I (Bottleneck Constant)
  - Non-distributive multiplication with corrective term Ω(I)
  - Supersymmetric framework via I² = I or I² = J
  - Physical applications to dark matter/energy (J-field)
  - Smooth singularity resolution in black holes
  - Hardware architecture for Floating-I arithmetic
  - Cryptographic systems based on paired-prime square roots
  
  INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY NOTICE:
  The Constant of the Bottleneck (I) and its algebraic framework are proprietary
  intellectual property linked to ORCID 0009-0006-6874-3910. Any implementation
  of indeterminate resolution (0/0 as a functional constant) in hardware, software,
  or AI systems requires explicit authorization.
